      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2ffaa2e4df5767fb1e91cb|full_name}: I understand this perspective. But in this scenario the conversation is about a *social* feature, that already has and will continue to make massive changes in coming months as to how people interact with one another.\n\nIt most definitely will be the primary way for how people will start finding new friends/communities, as well as keeping track of massive friend's list.\n\nA lot of people make massive amount of content for VRChat already, and quite a bit of them are and have been doing it for absolutely free. VRC+ has and will continue to be paid for by people that are able to afford it even if creating groups isn't paywalled.\n\nAt first the narrative was \"VRC+ Features are just a bonus, you pay to support developers.\" but now we are at the point where a *social* feature that will make a massive impact on community interactions as a whole - is gated behind a paywall and may affect interactions of people in a negative way because they are not able to afford VRC+.\n\nIn case they need to incentivize more people to subscribe, then that should be done in the way that *does not* limit ways for people to be social with each other.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
